  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the village of Port Dickinson, in the county of Broome, to offer an optional twenty year retirement plan to Sean D. Crouse and Paul Buttacovoli, Jr.",
    "basePrintNo": "S6813",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6813-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6813\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to authorize the village of Port Dickinson, in the county of\nBroome, to offer an optional twenty year retirement plan to Sean D.\nCrouse and Paul Buttacovoli, Jr.\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo make the benefits of section 384-d of the New York State and Local\nPolice and Fire Retirement System available to police officers Sean D.\nCrouse and Paul Buttacavoli Jr. who, for reasons not ascribable to\ntheir own negligence, failed to make a timely application to\nparticipate in such retirement plan.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 allows the Village of Port Dickinson to elect to reopen the\noptional twenty year retirement plan (section 384..d) for police\nofficers Sean D. Crouse and Paul Buttacavoli Jr.\n\nSection 2 requires the Village of Port Dickinson to pay for all\nemployer costs associated with reopening the plan.\n\nSection 3 contains the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis legislation is necessary to allow the Village of Port Dickinson\nto reopen the enrollment period for plan 384-d of the New York State\nand Local Police and Fire Retirement System for police officers Sean\nD. Crouse and Paul Buttacavoli Jr.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nThis bill would result in an increase of approximately $2100 in annual\ncontributions for the Village of Port Dickinson for the fiscal year\nending May 30, 2010 and a past service cost of approximately $51,600\nwhich would be borne by the Village of Port Dickinson over a ten year\nperiod.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
